  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Tote Services has $308M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 289 awards with an average award size of $1.1M. Tote Services obligations are up 22.9% year over year. Tote Services fiscal-year obligations swung from $726M in FY21 down to $157M in FY23, then rose to $207M in FY24, $251M in FY25, and $308M in FY26. Tote Services top buying agencies in FY2026 to date are the Department of Transportation with $254M and the Department of Defense with $54.8M. Tote Services largest markets by NAICS in FY2026 to date are Deep Sea Freight Transportation with $269M, Ship Building and Repairing with $39.4M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) with $500. The figures reported are contract obligations except where table notes indicate award-value totals for largest awards and expiring contracts, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Tote Services' federal business trended year over year?",
        "body": "Tote Services obligations fell from $726M in FY21 to $157M in FY23, then recovered to $207M in FY24 and $251M in FY25. Tote Services obligations reached $308M in FY26 to date, representing an increase of up 22.9% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Tote Services' top federal customers and which markets dominate?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation is the top buyer of Tote Services with $254M in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Defense with $54.8M. Deep Sea Freight Transportation is the dominant market at $269M, with Ship Building and Repairing at $39.4M and R&D in the physical, engineering, and life sciences at $500."
      }
    ]
  },
